      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A study of the characteristic changes of the cerebral blood circulation in patients with hypertensive disease after corinfar intakes indicates that the cerebral blood flow and self-feeling of the patients varied depending on the initial state of the cerebral blood flow. \"Hypotonic\" disorders of the cerebral blood flow are less favourable for corinfar treatment as compared with the \"spastic\" disturbances."},
